  [DATA] ABC3 (A,B,C) depth<=3 the J census: J=1 on 1476 closed squares, of which 0 have r != 1;  J=0 on 78 (66 with r = 1 and 12 defective);  squares with MIXED reverse-admissibility (exactly one endpoint): 0
  [DATA] (A,B) depth<=5 the J census: J=1 on 6026 closed squares, of which 0 have r != 1;  J=0 on 5788 (4828 with r = 1 and 960 defective);  squares with MIXED reverse-admissibility (exactly one endpoint): 0
  [DATA] AB4 J against the register invariant and against depth: J=1 AND register-OVERLAPPING: 793 squares (so J is not the register-disjointness invariant of A2.1 / D72 T2.3b); register-DISJOINT with J=0: 168; at total depth 4 alone, 912/1252 unit squares carry J=1 and 0/84 defective ones do
  [PASS] D9.1 THE REVERSAL-EVEN CHANNEL IS NOT EMPTY: J = 1 IMPLIES r = 1, AND J = 0 ON EVERY DEFECTIVE SQUARE.  This is round 1's find and it is credited as such — the raw material is this receipt's own D5 arm, which evaluated the predicate on the 88 defective squares and never on the complement.  Across three arms J = 1 on thousands of closed squares and EVERY ONE of them has holonomy exactly 1; every defective square in every arm has J = 0.  J is therefore a SUBSTRATE-SUPPLIED FLATNESS PREDICATE that locates the curvature, and it is reversal-EVEN — it neither inverts nor conjugates.  It is NOT a relabelling of the register invariant A2.1 already has (hundreds of register-OVERLAPPING squares carry J = 1, and register-DISJOINT squares carry J = 0), and it is not a depth artefact (it separates within the deepest stratum).  D8's second clause — 'every quantity this unit could build on these loops inverts under reversal' — is REFUTED by it.  [MEASURED] on three windows; NOT a theorem, and not licensed as one: whether J = 1 => r = 1 survives greater depth and wider pools is the successor's first question  (J=1 on 8600 closed squares across 3 arms with 0 exceptions to r = 1; J=0 on 1060/1060 defective squares; per arm  J=1 6026 (exceptions 0), J=0 5788 = 4828 unit + 960 defective; AB4 J=1 1098 (exceptions 0), J=0 448 = 360 unit + 88 defective; ABC3 J=1 1476 (exceptions 0), J=0 78 = 66 unit + 12 defective; mixed-endpoint squares 0 in every arm, so J is well defined as a symmetric predicate)
  [PASS] D8 THE ODD-SECTOR VERDICT: NO SCALAR ORIENTATION-SENSITIVE RESIDUE EXISTS ON THIS CARRIER.  Every SCALAR quantity this unit could build on the holonomy-carrying loops INVERTS under reversal; nothing CONJUGATES.  The negative is reported as loudly as a positive would have been, per the pin's sec.4: the imaginary exponential is not at this address either.  ROUND-1 SCOPE REPAIR: this is a statement about the SCALAR ODD sector — the U(1) part — and D2 settles it a priori in one line for a positive-rational connection.  It is NOT the statement that the reversal-even channel is empty; D9.1 exhibits a non-trivial invariant there  (unimodular values other than 1: []; order-dual conjugating (fixed) dual squares 0 of 0 in-family dual squares; i-twist informative = False (D4.1); the predicate's positive branch is demonstrated at OUT.1)
  [DATA] TH-D block time: 3s

